hello there video game developers have  taken each other's ideas countless times  throughout the history of gaming because  a good idea is a good idea epic games  and fortnite aren't above this either  and over the course of fortnite's  meteoric growth to where it is now  they've shall we say borrowed a few  concepts from their competitors i'm adam  maru here's my creator code if you're  interested and now sit your butt down  for 10 minutes while we uncover 16 times  fortnite stole from other games oh and  please don't see this as an attack on  epic it isn't i just want to see who  deserves the credit for the things we  love in fortnite  [Music]  okay let's start with the latest and  greatest example of this fortnight's  imposter game mode the moment we all saw  this we knew this was fortnite's among  us and it's impossible not to see the  similarities both modes have a team of  innocent parties completing tasks to win  the game and then there's two imposters  running around attempting to sabotage  and eliminate those innocent players the  tasks vary and the sabotages are  different but at its core it's the exact  same game epic simply took it i  personally prefer fortnite version 2  among us but credit where credit is due  among us did this first this story gets  a little more cutting when we found out  that the among us team had tried in vain  to speak to epic about a crossover  between the two games epic instead  decided to simply do it for themselves  leaving the originators feeling stabbed  in the back i still hold hope that a  crossover will be possible but a bridge  has definitely been burned between the  two companies  fortnite had everything going for it in  chapter one season four and five grew  the player base exponentially and  everything was rosy but suddenly on  february 4th 2019 a new battle royale  game appeared apex legends it took the  battle royale genre and added its own  spin and oh my gosh it scared the hell  out of epic games so much so that they  added multiple ideas from apex to keep  the lead in the br race one of the  biggest draws to apex was the ability to  pick up your teammate once they fell in  battle their hollow card banner could be  grabbed and rushed to the nearest  respawn beacon which would bring them  back from the clutches of death not only  is this a fun mechanic it also makes  players who may have been eliminated  earlier in the game still engage with it  and be part of the team epic saw this  and one day later yes just one day they  said this a new feature landing in  fortnite next week the reboot fan lose a  squad mate early in the match bring him  back and finish strong less than 24  hours that took i for one i'm glad they  did copy this mechanic because i die  die so much apex was a real contender in  2019 and the reboot vans were only the  start of things which fortnight borrowed  the thing we all take for granted when  playing today is the ping system marking  points of interest and weapons and  enemies and consumables this mechanic is  vital these days and it's tough to think  back to a time when it wasn't here that  so happens to be back when apex arrived  and their innovative one-button ping  system made communicating even without a  mic a complete breeze respawn received  heavy praise for this system and look  only a fortnight later see what i did  there it was in fortnite apex released  with a trio's game mode and it just so  happened that a few days before apex  became available epic was testing a trio  mode themselves this could be  coincidence or it could mean that they  had seen the closed testing for apex and  realized trios is a big deal and people  want to play it however you see this the  sweatiest mode in fortnite br is most  likely influenced by apex legends  [Music]  before battle royale took over the  gaming space there was another king of  games overwatch a hero shooter which  puts characters at the forefront with  personalities and defining  characteristics fortnight took  inspiration from these established  characters and straight up took them  made a couple of changes and sold them  to the community here's only a few of  them because this would take all day  overwatch's mercy is an angel complete  with halo and winks and a segmented  white dress and this is fortnite's ark  an angel complete with halo and wings  and a segmented white dress  that must be a coincidence right this is  overwatch's widow maker a  spider-inspired femme fatale and this is  fortnite's arachne a spider-inspired  femme fatale there's a theme here one of  my own kin tracer don't worry loves  cavalry's ear  looks a great deal like rocks they even  strike the same pose too and what about  a mega and genji i think you get the  idea what's your take on this have  fortnite been copying overwatch's  homework or is everything a coincidence  and good ideas are good ideas  fortnite has seen many copycats over the  years trying to build a reputation by  mimicking its success one of these games  was realm royale which introduced a  mechanic to select where on the island  you wanted to dive to it was great and  helped the whole squad know exactly  where they were going before they even  left the fake battle bus this was so  helpful in squad games that epic grabbed  this and applied it to fortnite and  eventually that became part of the ping  system we talked about earlier but this  wasn't the only time a copycat of  fortnite had the attention of epic games  did you ever play the creative  destruction game it's 100  a fortnight rip-off right down to the  cartoonish aesthetic but even this had  new ideas to add to the br formula one  of these was a weapon called the  destructor a two-handed weapon which  literally ripped apart the buildings in  front of you epic decided to take  inspiration from the game that took  inspiration from them and gave us the  recycler a weapon that could both rip  buildings to pieces and also fire them  at enemies the recycler's effective and  explosive attack will deal damage to  enemies and help you tear down their  builds other weapons and items have a  history before fortnite any team  fortress 2 fans in the house in team  fortress 2 the medic class can be chosen  and they use a bazooka-style weapon to  heal their teammates  does it look familiar that bazooka was  added to fortnite and shot out a steady  stream of bandages and when this was  iterated upon and the chug cannon was  released it looked even closer to the  original design found in team fortress  2.  epic have actually stolen from epic in  the past too let me explain all the  previous games they've worked on have  impacted fortnite in many ways for  example the original knocked animation  was taken from gears of war when they  made the original game before microsoft  moved that franchise to another team the  down but not out mechanic became so  loved by gamers that it's in most things  you play these days a second chance to  be revived and brought back into the  match if you saw my last video about  secrets in the new imposter game mode  you'll have seen me talk about the  infinity blade put simply infinity blade  assets were directly taken from that now  dead game and brought to life in  fortnite the rune language we all love  kevin the cube for isn't a new concept  at all it's been here all along in  infinity blade they just grabbed it and  put it in fortnite i don't think we can  call this theft this is more a reuse of  assets but it shows once again that  other games heavily inspire fortnite  right down to the mysteries of kevin the  cube  one last apex piece of thievery epic was  so worried by apex legends that they  decided to give away the season 8  fortnight battle pass for free to  everyone foregoing millions upon  millions of dollars to get people back  on board playing their game and it just  so happens that the tier 100 skin for  that season was this lady looks  and i hate to say this but she looks  heavily inspired by lifeline from apex  and once you see it it's hard to unsee  it from the way her clothes sit her skin  complexity and of course the signature  lifeline hair another thing apex  pioneered our emotes while skydiving and  two years later we are starting to see  them used in fortnite there's only one  right now do you know what it is it's  superman he's the only skin with a  totally unique diving animation with his  legendary pose hey i'm not saying  fortnite are taken from apex again but  if in a year's time we are all back  flipping out the battle bus i think we  know who to credit  there's a ton more we could talk about  so let's quickly give a few an honorable  mention fortnite introduced gold and  bounties after seeing the success of  cash and bounties in call of duty war  zone at the time that was their closest  competitor but it isn't always battle  royale they take from grabbing a chicken  in fortnite is actually taken from a  certain nintendo game which has had that  for years the legend of zelda traveling  far and wide quickly and safely has been  almost perfectly recreated in fortnite i  think we can safely say the developers  of fortnite play a lot of video games so  there we have it 16 times epic stole  ideas to improve fortnite wherever you  sit on this subject i think it's  important to applaud the games that  inspired the current fortnite world and  in particular games like apex legends  that push epic into evolving their game  for future years now though i throw this  to you can you tell me any games that  have stolen from fortnite and let's make  a video of the other side of this  argument what do you say i'm adam you're  awesome here's a bunch of legends who  are kind enough to use code adamara in  the store thank you so much you keep me  going every week much appreciated i'll  see you next time  [Music]  you
 

